Focus-view motion vectors (DCS Control, 2026-11-26): [ofxr] dcs_motion_focus, the consumer of motion contract revision 4
(patch 0127; docs/FOCUS_MOTION.md). Off by default; experimental.
- CockpitMaskConsumer (option dcs_motion_focus): with a revision 4 producer that publishes them, the focus views 2 / 3
  (view_record, view_usable, true_motion_view: their jitter must be proven per view) join the frame's one MV / class copy,
  and the per-pixel depth plane (R16_FLOAT, depth_usable) is opened with the generation and copied in the same list
  under the one fence wait (D3D12CockpitMaskFrame::motion_focus_views, motion_depth_texture). A plane shared after the
  generation was opened opens that generation again once. Stats: motion_focus_paired, motion_depth_paired,
  motion_focus_refused.
- D3D12FrameSynthesizer (D3D12NvidiaOpticalFlowOptions::dcs_motion_focus): a pair whose current frame has a focus view's
  MVs resamples on a 4 px grid (its own target and scatter where the image's cell is coarser; the view blocks' t11 / t12
  rewritten per slot only when the grid changes). dcs_motion.hlsl: cells inside the focus inset (by tangent; the whole
  image of a focus layer's swapchain) take the focus view's MVs with an edge-aware filter (bilinear over the texels of
  the nearest texel's surface only: class, depth within 3 % + 0.25 m, motion within about one output pixel) and the
  same rules for the one-surface test; a one-cell feather at the inset's edge; cells outside take the periphery cell
  of today's size they lie in, computed exactly as before (duplicated on the fine grid). frame_synthesis.hlsl:
  UseGameMotion bit 9 (fine grid) and bits 10-11 (the periphery's cell) keep dcs_motion_sky_occlusion's search reach.
- Key off, or no focus MVs in the pair (an older producer, unproven jitter, F10): the resample, the grid and every
  composition exactly as before (fixture-checked byte for byte).
- Tests: cockpit_mask_tests test_motion_focus_revision4; xrfg_d3d12_fg_focus_motion (tests/fg_focus_motion.inc,
  XRFG_TEST_FG_FOCUS_MOTION=1[,x4][,d1]); XRFG_TEST_DCS_MOTION_BENCH_FOCUS=1 with the MV bench;
  XRFG_TEST_DCS_MOTION_CELL (from 0120) forces the image's cell in tests.
